***************************** T A L Y S **************************7925 1451  184
                                                                  7925 1451  185
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   7925 1451  186
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      7925 1451  187
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    7925 1451  188
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     7925 1451  189
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  7925 1451  190
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        7925 1451  191
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    7925 1451  192
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         7925 1451  193
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      7925 1451  194
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    7925 1451  195
stored in this data file:                                         7925 1451  196
                                                                  7925 1451  197
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   7925 1451  198
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     7925 1451  199
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 7925 1451  200
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   7925 1451  201
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                7925 1451  202
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   7925 1451  203
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    7925 1451  204
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        7925 1451  205
- Recoil data                                                     7925 1451  206
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           7925 1451  207
- Total particle energy spectra                                   7925 1451  208
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      7925 1451  209
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        7925 1451  210
- Residual production cross sections                              7925 1451  211
                                                                  7925 1451  212
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            7925 1451  213
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        7925 1451  214
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   7925 1451  215
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                7925 1451  216
                                                                  7925 1451  217
