##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    7925 1451  220
                                                                  7925 1451  221
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       7925 1451  222
                                                                  7925 1451  223
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          7925 1451  224
                                                                  7925 1451  225
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   7925 1451  226
                                                                  7925 1451  227
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 7925 1451  228
                                                                  7925 1451  229
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     7925 1451  230
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   7925 1451  231
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             7925 1451  232
                                                                  7925 1451  233
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                7925 1451  234
                                                                  7925 1451  235
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       7925 1451  236
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  7925 1451  237
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   7925 1451  238
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  7925 1451  239
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  7925 1451  240
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 7925 1451  241
to the highest incident energy.                                   7925 1451  242
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:7925 1451  243
                                                                  7925 1451  244
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  7925 1451  245
                                                                  7925 1451  246
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    7925 1451  247
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     7925 1451  248
                                                                  7925 1451  249
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     7925 1451  250
                                                                  7925 1451  251
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    7925 1451  252
total cross section.                                              7925 1451  253
                                                                  7925 1451  254
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            7925 1451  255
                                                                  7925 1451  256
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    7925 1451  257
                                                                  7925 1451  258
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        7925 1451  259
                                                                  7925 1451  260
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  7925 1451  261
                                                                  7925 1451  262
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           7925 1451  263
                                                                  7925 1451  264
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   7925 1451  265
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        7925 1451  266
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     7925 1451  267
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         7925 1451  268
sections.                                                         7925 1451  269
                                                                  7925 1451  270
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 7925 1451  271
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 7925 1451  272
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 7925 1451  273
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 7925 1451  274
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      7925 1451  275
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       7925 1451  276
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              7925 1451  277
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  7925 1451  278
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  7925 1451  279
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  7925 1451  280
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  7925 1451  281
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  7925 1451  282
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       7925 1451  283
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        7925 1451  284
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        7925 1451  285
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        7925 1451  286
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        7925 1451  287
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        7925 1451  288
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        7925 1451  289
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        7925 1451  290
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       7925 1451  291
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        7925 1451  292
                                                                  7925 1451  293
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           7925 1451  294
                                                                  7925 1451  295
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    7925 1451  296
discrete levels.                                                  7925 1451  297
                                                                  7925 1451  298
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         7925 1451  299
                                                                  7925 1451  300
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  7925 1451  301
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   7925 1451  302
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      7925 1451  303
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  7925 1451  304
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      7925 1451  305
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         7925 1451  306
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   7925 1451  307
on an angular grid.                                               7925 1451  308
                                                                  7925 1451  309
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       7925 1451  310
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        7925 1451  311
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         7925 1451  312
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         7925 1451  313
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         7925 1451  314
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        7925 1451  315
                                                                  7925 1451  316
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     7925 1451  317
                                                                  7925 1451  318
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     7925 1451  319
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   7925 1451  320
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  7925 1451  321
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             7925 1451  322
All data are generated with TALYS.                                7925 1451  323
                                                                  7925 1451  324
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   7925 1451  325
                                                                  7925 1451  326
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      7925 1451  327
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   7925 1451  328
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   7925 1451  329
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are7925 1451  330
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   7925 1451  331
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  7925 1451  332
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              7925 1451  333
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 7925 1451  334
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  7925 1451  335
For each residual product:                                        7925 1451  336
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               7925 1451  337
- the recoil                                                      7925 1451  338
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         7925 1451  339
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     7925 1451  340
sections.                                                         7925 1451  341
                                                                  7925 1451  342
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     7925 1451  343
                                                                  7925 1451  344
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  7925 1451  345
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 7925 1451  346
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          7925 1451  347
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       7925 1451  348
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 7925 1451  349
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     7925 1451  350
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  7925 1451  351
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      7925 1451  352
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         7925 1451  353
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             7925 1451  354
                                                                  7925 1451  355
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   7925 1451  356
followed:                                                         7925 1451  357
                                                                  7925 1451  358
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         7925 1451  359
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         7925 1451  360
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         7925 1451  361
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     7925 1451  362
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7925 1451  363
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7925 1451  364
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7925 1451  365
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7925 1451  366
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7925 1451  367
                                                                  7925 1451  368
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 7925 1451  369
                                                                  7925 1451  370
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    7925 1451  371
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          7925 1451  372
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     7925 1451  373
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          7925 1451  374
                                                                  7925 1451  375
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  7925 1451  376
                                                                  7925 1451  377
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     7925 1451  378
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    7925 1451  379
as isomer.                                                        7925 1451  380
                                                                  7925 1451  381
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 7925 1451  382
                                                                  7925 1451  383
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        7925 1451  384
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    7925 1451  385
as isomer.                                                        7925 1451  386
                                                                  7925 1451  387
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          7925 1451  388
                                                                  7925 1451  389
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:7925 1451  390
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   7925 1451  391
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   7925 1451  392
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   7925 1451  393
  given                                                           7925 1451  394
                                                                  7925 1451  395
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          7925 1451  396
                                                                  7925 1451  397
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  7925 1451  398
                                                                  7925 1451  399
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 7925 1451  400
                                                                  7925 1451  401
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         7925 1451  402
                                                                  7925 1451  403
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   7925 1451  404
                                                                  7925 1451  405
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        7925 1451  406
and more details are given above in this description. In most     7925 1451  407
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        7925 1451  408
                                                                  7925 1451  409
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 7925 1451  410
                                                                  7925 1451  411
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  7925 1451  412
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     7925 1451  413
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    7925 1451  414
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   7925 1451  415
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  7925 1451  416
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                7925 1451  417
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      7925 1451  418
   same reaction channel between different energies)              7925 1451  419
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      7925 1451  420
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               7925 1451  421
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      7925 1451  422
   different reaction channels for different energies)            7925 1451  423
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        7925 1451  424
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              7925 1451  425
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  7925 1451  426
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       7925 1451  427
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     7925 1451  428
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  7925 1451  429
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     7925 1451  430
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     7925 1451  431
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     7925 1451  432
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   7925 1451  433
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   7925 1451  434
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  7925 1451  435
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   7925 1451  436
                                                                  7925 1451  437
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  7925 1451  438
                                                                  7925 1451  439
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       7925 1451  440
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  7925 1451  441
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       7925 1451  442
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   7925 1451  443
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         7925 1451  444
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  7925 1451  445
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      7925 1451  446
representation is used.                                           7925 1451  447
                                                                  7925 1451  448
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      7925 1451  449
                                                                  7925 1451  450
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  7925 1451  451
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             7925 1451  452
                                                                  7925 1451  453
